# Yeoon & Company Website

- This repository contains the corporate website for Yeoon & Company.
- The current product is a static company website built with Next.js and deployed through AWS Amplify.
- Explain work to the user in Korean. Keep source code, identifiers, commit messages, and developer documentation in English unless the user requests otherwise.
- Do not invent company history, customers, partnerships, product capabilities, launch dates, legal compliance, financial compliance, certifications, contact details, or performance claims.
- Clearly label planned products and unverified features as planned, in development, or under validation.
- Keep Yeoon & Company distinct from Yeoon Law Firm in branding, content, navigation, and contact flows.
- Never expose or commit credentials, private keys, AWS access keys, production environment values, or personal data.
- Preserve existing user changes. Before deleting files, changing dependencies, or changing deployment configuration, explain the target and expected impact.

## Browser and CDP Boundary

- Do not launch, control, inspect, or automate a browser unless the user explicitly requests browser-based work.
- Do not use Chrome DevTools Protocol (CDP), Chrome DevTools, Browser Automation, Playwright, Puppeteer, or browser MCP tools without explicit user approval in the current request.
- Do not start a local development server or perform browser-based visual verification unless explicitly requested.
